{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Who said of his father and of his mother, 'I have not seen him.'</b> When they sinned with the calf and I said, ״Who is for YHWH, to me״ (Exodus 32), all the children of Levi gathered to me, and I commanded them to kill — his mother's father, and he is an Israelite, or his mother's brother, or his daughter's son — and so they did. And it is impossible to explain his actual father and his father's brother and likewise his actual sons, for they are Levites, and from the tribe of Levi not one of them sinned, as it says (there) ״all the children of Levi״." "<b>For they kept Your word.</b> ״You shall have no other elohim״ (Exodus 20:2)." "<b>And Your covenant they preserved.</b> The covenant of circumcision — for those of Israel who were born in the wilderness did not circumcise their sons, and they [the Levites] were circumcised and circumcised their sons."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:41.049557728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}